@startuml SolanaProgramsLifecycleSeq1
' REVIEWED_MAIN_2026_05_13: aligned to current merged code; large-investment retained pending simplification merge.

title Corda Protocol V1 – Solana Programs Deployment & Admin Lifecycle (Squads v4 Multisig 2-of-4)

autonumber "<b>##"

box "Governance Actors" #LightGray
actor "Deployer\n(ephemeral key)" as DEP
actor "Signer 1" as S1
actor "Signer 2" as S2
actor "Signer 3" as S3
actor "Signer 4" as S4
end box

box "Solana On-chain" #DFF3FF
participant "Squads v4 Program\n(2-of-4 multisig)" as SQ
participant "Vault Program" as VP
database "On-chain State\n(Programs + PDAs)" as CHAIN
end box

note over DEP,S4
Ephemeral deployer key used only for the deployment ceremony.
Squads multisig (2-of-4) governs upgrade authority post-handover.
Admin keys are set at initialization and are NOT rotatable.
end note

== Phase 1: Squads Multisig Setup ==

S2 -> S1: <color brown>**DF_SHARE_MEMBER_PUBKEY**</color>\nShare signer public key
S3 -> S1: <color brown>**DF_SHARE_MEMBER_PUBKEY**</color>\nShare signer public key
S4 -> S1: <color brown>**DF_SHARE_MEMBER_PUBKEY**</color>\nShare signer public key
S1 -> S1: <color brown>**DF_VALIDATE_MEMBER_PUBKEYS**</color>\nVerify key ownership\n(out-of-band challenge signature)

S1 -> SQ: <color brown>**DF_REGISTER_MULTISIG**</color>\nCreate multisig (createKey + 4 members + threshold=2)
SQ -> CHAIN: Persist multisig PDA, member pubkeys, roles, threshold

note over SQ,CHAIN
Squads v4 roles per member:
- Proposer, Voter, Executor
Role segregation enforced to prevent
single-member proposal+approval+execution.
end note

== Phase 2: Program Deployment (Ephemeral Deployer Key) ==

note over DEP
Deployer generates fresh keypairs per program.
target/deploy/*-keypair.json determines program IDs.
These keypairs must NEVER exist on dev laptops.
end note

DEP -> VP: <color brown>**DF_DEPLOY_PROGRAMS**</color>\nDeploy Vault program
VP -> CHAIN: Write program code (upgrade authority = deployer)

note over DEP,CHAIN #FFCCCC
**BOOTSTRAP WINDOW (CRITICAL)**
Deployer holds unilateral upgrade authority.
Minimize this window. No operational use until handover completes.
end note

== Phase 3: Upgrade Authority Handover ==

DEP -> VP: <color brown>**DF_AUTHORITY_HANDOVER**</color>\nSetAuthority → Squads PDA

DEP -> DEP: <color red>**Retire ephemeral deployer key**</color>\n(securely destroy)

note over DEP,CHAIN
After handover, only the Squads multisig PDA
can authorize program upgrades.
Deployer key is permanently retired.
end note

== Phase 4: Program Initialization ==

note over S1,CHAIN
Initialization sets the permanent vault admin key.
These calls are separate from upgrade authority.
end note

S1 -> VP: <color brown>**DF_INITIALIZE_PROGRAMS**</color>\ninitialize_vault(admin=<admin_key>, ...)
VP -> CHAIN: Create Vault PDA, set admin, mints, accounts

== Phase 5: Post-Deployment Verification ==

S1 -> CHAIN: <color brown>**DF_VERIFY_DEPLOYMENT**</color>\nVerify vault program ID
S2 -> CHAIN: <color brown>**DF_VERIFY_DEPLOYMENT**</color>\nIndependently verify code hashes

S1 -> CHAIN: Verify upgrade authority == Squads PDA
S2 -> CHAIN: Verify admin key == approved address
S1 -> CHAIN: Verify vault ACL/oracle-wrapper compatibility

alt All verifications passed
    S1 -> S1: Record governance note (deployment valid)
    S1 -> S1: Enable operational use
else Any verification failed
    S1 -> SQ: Raise incident, block operational use
end

== Runtime: Admin Operations (Non-Multisig, Single-Key) ==

note over S1,CHAIN #FFFFCC
Admin operations use a single signing key,
NOT the Squads multisig. These keys are non-rotatable.
end note

S1 -> VP: Vault admin: add_to_vtoken_whitelist(wallet)
VP -> CHAIN: Create/update VaultWhitelistEntry PDA

S1 -> VP: Vault admin: update_vault_config(...)
VP -> CHAIN: Update curator, thresholds, fees

S1 -> VP: Vault admin: pause() [emergency]
VP -> CHAIN: Set is_paused = true

== Runtime: Governed Program Upgrade ==

S1 -> SQ: <color brown>**DF_UPGRADE_PROGRAMS**</color>\nPropose upgrade (e.g., Vault program)
SQ -> SQ: Record proposal (status: pending)

S2 -> SQ: Vote approve
SQ -> SQ: Quorum reached (2-of-4)

S3 -> SQ: Execute proposal (invoke_signed)
SQ -> VP: <color brown>**DF_UPGRADE_PROGRAMS**</color>\nUpgrade instruction via BPF Loader
VP -> CHAIN: Replace program code from buffer

S1 -> CHAIN: Verify upgraded code hash
S2 -> CHAIN: Independently confirm artifact match

== Optional: Transition to Immutability ==

note over S1,CHAIN
Lock sequence respects cross-program dependencies:
1. Verify vault dependencies and state bindings
2. Lock vault in a controlled step
end note

S2 -> SQ: <color brown>**DF_IMMUTABLE_LOCK**</color>\nPropose immutable lock (Vault)
S3 -> SQ: Vote approve
SQ -> VP: <color brown>**DF_IMMUTABLE_LOCK**</color>\nRevoke upgrade authority
VP -> CHAIN: Upgrade authority = None (permanent)

note over VP,CHAIN #FFCCCC
After immutable lock, no further code upgrades are possible.
Admin operations still function (single-key, non-rotatable).
If admin key is compromised post-lock, there is NO recovery path.
end note

== Attempted Upgrade After Lock ==

S1 -> SQ: Propose upgrade (post-lock)
S2 -> SQ: Vote approve
SQ -> VP: Execute upgrade attempt
VP --> SQ: **Reject** (program is immutable)

== Multisig Membership Changes ==

S1 -> SQ: <color brown>**DF_MEMBER_UPDATE**</color>\nPropose add/remove member
S2 -> SQ: Vote approve
SQ -> CHAIN: Update multisig member list

note over S1,CHAIN
Membership changes affect upgrade governance only.
On-chain admin keys are unaffected
(non-rotatable, set at initialization).
end note

@enduml
